{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - IAM - Resourceset - Okta Custom Admin Role or Resource Set Changed",
	"Description": "A custom administrator role, its permissions, or a resource set binding was changed. Custom roles are how Okta does fine-grained delegated administration, so adding a permission to a role or binding a role to a wider resource set escalates privilege without ever touching the standard admin roles.\n\nEvent types: iam.role.create, iam.role.update, iam.role.permissions.add, iam.resourceset.create, iam.resourceset.update, iam.resourceset.bindings.add, iam.resourceset.resources.add\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/CustomRole/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
